        "stageRecord": "Blev raises from the upper verbal head to finite I, leaving a head trace in the auxiliary VP. The resulting complex I head contains the overt, already inflected auxiliary and the silent abstract tense head. This explicitly adopts a V-to-I-to-C derivation of the Swedish finite verb rather than base-generating blev in C or skipping the intervening inflectional head. No morphological decomposition or additional surface realization is introduced: blev remains one whole-word terminal. The subject remains in Spec-IP, and its object trace remains inside the participial predicate.",
